  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Piperacillin is an extended-spectrum penicillin antibiotic used to treat bacterial infections such as sepsis, urinary tract, skin, and respiratory infections, including Pseudomonas and E. coli infections. It is an approved medicine, typically given by infusion, and is often combined with tazobactam in hospital settings.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q423787&quot;>Wikidata Q423787</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>piperacillin</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>J01CA12</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB00319&quot;>DB00319</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/43672&quot;>43672</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:8232&quot;>8232</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q423787&quot;>Q423787</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C23H27N5O7S</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>517.557 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
